{"id": "EUVD-2026-93338", "enisaUuid": "6a5caf66-3551-3fcd-b2fd-d17d1ca9a76d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/erdma: Use IRQ-safe XArray helpers for QP and CQ tables\n\nLocked QP and CQ lookups from EQ interrupts can deadlock with\ncreate-path XArray updates. If an interrupt arrives while the create\npath holds the plain xa_lock, the lookup spins forever trying to\nacquire the same lock.\n\nUse IRQ-safe XArray helpers for all QP and CQ create-path updates,\nincluding the GSI QP store and error paths. Initialize both arrays with\nXA_FLAGS_LOCK_IRQ so sleeping allocations preserve interrupt state.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e32aa1d85126e6d5ef6efd594ced3f75178886ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/74d4085221a7ec5440996af199ccadfa75b9eb0e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/00baeade709fb66da647e8327e8398bb532e30f7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c26j-r98f-9j66", "CVE-2026-98353"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "299d8d6a-ee7b-318f-80e9-14ca48def1c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "98df2aee1459ee1c62c70cbe9b370d2a532aea36 <00baeade709fb66da647e8327e8398bb532e30f7"}, {"id": "351a9d03-2099-36d1-8942-fbdecdb38639", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.110 <6.13"}, {"id": "3ff42156-ac71-368e-a525-bd6e4b2b08ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.160 <6.7"}, {"id": "473a5761-4eb8-3f47-9efd-f50325375e6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6e32f84b63c054e09392153125d7202abab2d14b"}, {"id": "671d2ec7-9c8c-3bbf-a4ab-6f9d130faa6d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1fc9c1933959d2776a1ce7bf424251b8b5b586cd <e32aa1d85126e6d5ef6efd594ced3f75178886ce"}, {"id":